cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it. Once a Zenodo record exists, cite that record (DOI) rather than this repository."
title: "Protein Engineering Grammar: From Molecular Formats to Programmable Medicines"
abstract: "Protein therapeutics are conventionally classified by structural format: monoclonal, bispecific, conjugate, fusion. This scheme describes what a molecule is built from, not the functional logic it implements. We present a complementary vocabulary, the Protein Engineering Grammar, that describes an engineered protein as a modular information-processing system."
authors:
  - family-names: "Saka"
    given-names: "Koichiro"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
